We sit at the small dining table.
The food tastes fantastic.
I tell Nele that the food tastes very good to me.
We eat and talk.
For the first time, we do not talk about work.
Nele asks me if I like Berlin.
I answer her that I feel very comfortable here.
"I find that Berlin is slowly becoming my home," I say.
Nele smiles and takes a sip of water.
She says that she is very happy about that.
Then she asks what I do in my free time.
I tell her about my badminton club.
I explain that we play every Thursday evening.
"I will also play this Thursday," I add.
Nele finds that very interesting.
She plays tennis herself, but she has little time right now.
"Maybe I will come to badminton with you soon," she says.
I think that that is a great idea.
